# Data is regenerable from the pipeline — never committed (can be 100s of MB
# citywide). The committed pilot test fixture lives in tests/fixtures/, NOT
# here — data/tiles/ must hold only real production tiles, so nothing the
# tests depend on ever loads into the production server by accident.
data/*

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Secrets — uv auto-loads this at run time; never commit it (SOCRATA_APP_TOKEN)
.env

# Frontend (arrives in M4)
node_modules/
web/dist/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Claude Code local (per-machine) state — settings, plans, scheduled-task locks
.claude/

# Every .md file is a personal/working note and stays OUT of git -- the sole
# exception is the public README. This un-anchored *.md (with the README
# negation) covers, at any depth and automatically as new ones appear:
#   - CLAUDE.md, incl. nested per-area ones (web/CLAUDE.md, any future
#     server//pipeline/ equivalent) -- these MUST stay in place, Claude Code
#     auto-loads them by walking the tree; they are ignored, never moved.
#   - PLAN.md (current state/next steps), HISTORY.md + history/ (the narrative
#     it indexes), FIXES.md (open-bug punch list), REFETCH.md (per-refetch
#     rituals), EXTERNAL_AUDIT.md, and any ad-hoc note (accessibility-audit.md).
# If a doc ever SHOULD be tracked (a committed spec, an ADR), add its own
# `!path` negation alongside README's below.
*.md
!README.md
history/
